          <note>aar export: not expressible in FCPXML (see the export report)
outro.audio_track: outro sound is on the clip's own track (imported A1), not on A5 'A5' as planned; FCPXML cannot move a clip's sound to another track without doubling it in Resolve
template: FCPXML builds a new timeline; it does not start from template 'CCN Longform Template', so its tracks, buses, Fusion titles and settings are not carried
audio_tracks[0].mute: A1 'A1' is muted in the plan; exported audible (the CCN topology feeds the bus from muted tracks, so sound is never dropped)
audio_tracks[0].bus: A1 'A1' feeds bus 'A5'; FCPXML has no buses or Fairlight routing
audio_tracks[1].mute: A2 'A2' is muted in the plan; exported audible (the CCN topology feeds the bus from muted tracks, so sound is never dropped)
audio_tracks[1].bus: A2 'A2' feeds bus 'A5'; FCPXML has no buses or Fairlight routing
audio_tracks[2].mute: A3 'A3' is muted in the plan; exported audible (the CCN topology feeds the bus from muted tracks, so sound is never dropped)
audio_tracks[2].bus: A3 'A3' feeds bus 'A5'; FCPXML has no buses or Fairlight routing
audio_tracks[3].mute: A4 'A4' is muted in the plan; exported audible (the CCN topology feeds the bus from muted tracks, so sound is never dropped)
audio_tracks[3].bus: A4 'A4' feeds bus 'A5'; FCPXML has no buses or Fairlight routing
audio tracks after import:
plan A1 (A1) -&gt; imported A1
plan A5 (A5) -&gt; imported A1
split crossfades (transitions[0]): the overlap goes on another audio track (observed: A1 holds the later clip's sound)</note>
